WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.627
Zann tiptoed through a small cavern and into another tunnel.

2
00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:07.972
"I think the intersection is just ahead," he whispered to Zing.

3
00:00:07.973 --> 00:00:13.967
Zing breathed out a small flame, allowing Zann to see a little farther than the crawler's feeble glow permitted.

4
00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:17.349
There was no intersection—just a blank stone wall.

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.614
"Drat," Zann muttered.

6
00:00:19.615 --> 00:00:22.246
He retraced his steps and tried a different tunnel.

7
00:00:22.247 --> 00:00:25.972
Why hadn't he paid more attention when Tok was leading them out earlier?

8
00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:30.887
"Never mind," Zann whispered. At least he'd managed to sneak away undetected.

9
00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:35.949
Or had he? Zann froze as he heard a soft scraping sound behind him.

10
00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.542
It echoed down the tunnel, barely louder than a heartbeat.

11
00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:42.523
"Did you hear that?" he whispered to Zing.

12
00:00:42.524 --> 00:00:45.209
But apparently Zing hadn't heard the sound.

13
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.458
The dragon was staring at Zann's crawler hungrily.

14
00:00:48.459 --> 00:00:52.432
Zann sighed. Being in the creepy cave was making him jumpy.

15
00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:57.966
The sound had probably been nothing more than a cave creature or a stray burst of magic energy.

16
00:00:57.967 --> 00:01:01.596
Zann kept moving, watching for anything that looked familiar.

17
00:01:01.597 --> 00:01:02.335
Clink!

18
00:01:02.336 --> 00:01:06.073
Zann froze. Was that a footstep?

19
00:01:06.074 --> 00:01:10.318
"Quiet!" he hissed, dragging Zing into a crevasse in the wall.

20
00:01:10.319 --> 00:01:14.096
He pressed both hands over his crawler, trying to block its light.

21
00:01:14.097 --> 00:01:18.676
Zing's breath felt hot on Zann's leg, but Zann didn't dare move.

22
00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:23.112
The footsteps came closer. Soon Zann could hear the sound of breathing.

23
00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:26.444
He pressed himself back against the stone and watched.

24
00:01:26.445 --> 00:01:32.501
A figure passed, lit only by the soft glow of the crawler perched on its shoulder.

25
00:01:32.502 --> 00:01:34.868
"Perda!" Zann blurted out.

26
00:01:34.869 --> 00:01:40.591
Perda jumped in surprise and spun to face him. "Zann! I was afraid I'd lost you."

27
00:01:40.592 --> 00:01:43.722
Zann frowned. "You were following me?"

28
00:01:43.723 --> 00:01:52.070
"Of course." Perda laughed. "You didn't think you could sneak off and have another adventure without me, did you?"

29
00:01:52.071 --> 00:01:56.015
"But I was sure nobody saw me leave," said Zann.

30
00:01:56.016 --> 00:01:59.632
"You're right. I didn't notice you were gone for a few minutes.

31
00:01:59.633 --> 00:02:02.098
I used my crawler to track you."

32
00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:06.057
Perda pointed to her crawler, which was keeping a wary eye on Zing.

33
00:02:06.058 --> 00:02:10.422
"I'd already noticed it gets more and more nervous the closer we are to Zing.

34
00:02:10.423 --> 00:02:17.796
All I had to do was pay attention to how deeply its claws were digging into my shoulder to guess how close you were."

35
00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:22.628
Zann rolled his eyes. At the same time, he had to admire Perda's cleverness.

36
00:02:22.629 --> 00:02:26.731
"You have to go back," he told her. "It's too risky.

37
00:02:26.732 --> 00:02:32.425
Besides, maybe you can figure out a way to delay the Sealing spell until I'm finished."

38
00:02:32.426 --> 00:02:37.793
"Don't worry about that," Perda said. "The adults will be arguing for a while yet.

39
00:02:37.794 --> 00:02:40.814
Venna showed up right after you disappeared.

40
00:02:40.815 --> 00:02:45.346
She admitted to taking the relics. Most of them anyway."

41
00:02:45.347 --> 00:02:49.768
Zann was stunned. "Venna took the relics? Why?"

42
00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.296
"She doesn't think it's right to seal off the Cave and all the powerful magic in the relics.

43
00:02:54.297 --> 00:02:57.961
She thinks we should take some of the relics back to First City.

44
00:02:57.962 --> 00:03:03.358
That way the Red Council can use them in case a threat like Morb ever comes along again."

45
00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:09.398
"Wow." Zann knew how persuasive Venna could be. "Does anyone agree with her?"

46
00:03:09.399 --> 00:03:13.482
"A few people." Perda shrugged. "Not Boz and Teplo, though.

47
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:17.003
They'll all be arguing about it for a long time."

48
00:03:17.004 --> 00:03:21.899
"Good," Zann said. "That will give me enough time to find the message chamber."

49
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:26.406
"You mean it'll give us enough time," Perda said.

50
00:03:26.407 --> 00:03:29.404
"If you don't let me come, you'll never get there.

51
00:03:29.405 --> 00:03:32.992
You've been going the wrong way for the past ten minutes.

52
00:03:32.993 --> 00:03:35.781
Fortunately I remember how to get there.

53
00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:39.519
It's back this way." Perda quickly headed down the tunnel.

54
00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:43.526
Zann hurried to keep up with her. He was still annoyed that she'd followed him.

55
00:03:43.527 --> 00:03:46.194
But another part of him was glad to have her help.

56
00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:49.481
Half an hour later, they stepped into the message chamber.

57
00:03:49.482 --> 00:03:54.848
"Hurry," Perda urged. "Who knows how long we have until they start the Sealing spell.

58
00:03:54.849 --> 00:03:57.399
Then we'll be trapped in here forever."

59
00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:03.586
Zann’s stone was still burning hot. He took a deep breath and plugged it into the wall.

60
00:04:03.587 --> 00:04:07.899
"Oh!" he gasped as two figures appeared before him.

61
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.896
"Is that your parents?" Perda whispered.

62
00:04:10.897 --> 00:04:13.594
Zann just nodded, taking in the sight.

63
00:04:13.595 --> 00:04:19.747
"Greetings, Wyssa," his father's familiar voice said. "We received your last message."

64
00:04:19.748 --> 00:04:26.450
"We accept your terms," Zann's mother added. "We're very eager to locate World X.

65
00:04:26.451 --> 00:04:30.357
If you're sure you can lead us there, we'll pay your fee."

66
00:04:30.358 --> 00:04:39.586
Zann's father nodded. "We've just returned from the Cave of the Unknown and have one more short trip to make. We'll contact you when we return."

67
00:04:39.587 --> 00:04:42.662
Zann was so overwhelmed he could barely move.

68
00:04:42.663 --> 00:04:46.628
His parents' holograms flickered out and then reappeared.

69
00:04:46.629 --> 00:04:49.615
"Greetings, Wyssa . . . " the message began again.

70
00:04:49.616 --> 00:04:55.965
"Wow," Perda said. "I—ouch!" She poked her crawler. It was trembling.

71
00:04:55.966 --> 00:05:00.090
Zann realized his own crawler was digging its claws into his shoulder.

72
00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:04.827
"What's the matter with the crawlers?" he mumbled, still watching his parents.

73
00:05:04.828 --> 00:05:10.460
"They seem nervous," said Perda. "And Zing isn't even trying to eat them right now."

74
00:05:10.461 --> 00:05:17.128
The entire chamber shuddered. The message stone popped out of the wall, cutting off the hologram.

75
00:05:17.129 --> 00:05:20.440
"Uh-oh," Perda said. "Did you feel that?

76
00:05:20.441 --> 00:05:26.001
The Magic Masters must be starting the Sealing spell. We have to get out of here!"

77
00:05:26.002 --> 00:05:32.871
Zann didn't want to leave. He wanted to plug the stone back in and watch his parents' message again and again.

78
00:05:32.872 --> 00:05:38.715
There was another rumble. Zing let out a squeak. Zann's crawler moaned with fear.

79
00:05:38.716 --> 00:05:41.611
"Okay, let's go," Zann said.

80
00:05:41.612 --> 00:05:44.954
With Zing flying ahead of her, Perda ran for the exit.

81
00:05:44.955 --> 00:05:48.509
Zann started to follow. Suddenly he paused.

82
00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.515
Turning, he raced over and grabbed the message stone off the floor.

83
00:05:52.516 --> 00:05:57.093
Then he sprinted after Zing and Perda.

